ts: [tmpfiles.org/dl/wJwbpnwoMewP](https://tmpfiles.org/dl/wJwbpnwoMewP/master_prompts_from_db_26_sept_07.00_am.csv)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Resolved Incidents\n1. **ChatGPT UI Change & Reactive Send Button Fix:**\n   - Problem: In `worker_server.py`, Playwright's `active_page.keyboard.insert_text(req.prompt)` inserted text, but ChatGPT's React state didn't update, leaving the send button disabled. The fallback pressed `Control+Enter`, which did nothing because React saw the input as empty.\n   - Resolution: Added Space then Backspace keypresses to force React's input event to fire, updated send button selectors to include `button[aria-label*='Send' i]` and `button[data-testid*='send' i]`, and changed the fallback key from `Control+Enter` to `Enter`.\n2. **Assistant Turn DOM Extraction Resiliency:**\n   - Problem: ChatGPT changed its DOM structure so that `div[data-message-author-role=\"assistant\"]` and `article` sometimes returned 0 elements, causing `ChatGPT stream completed but no output text could be captured`.\n   - Resolution: Enhanced `worker_server.py` turn detection to support multi-selector queries (`article[data-testid*=\"conversation-turn-\"]`, `[data-message-author-role=\"assistant\"]`, `.markdown`, `[class*=\"markdown\" i]`), and updated turn validation so responses are correctly extracted even on fresh conversation URLs (`/c/<id>`).\n3. **Partition Completion:**\n   - Worker 3 (Irak Iroan AI, 8003) fully completed 100% of its assigned partition (Elements 62 to 81)! All ideas, prompts, and SEO are done for this range.\n4. **Container Memory & Busy Reset (429):**\n   - When a worker encounters `HTTP Error 429: Too Many Requests` due to lingering `is_busy: True` in FastAPI or DOM memory bloat, running `sg docker -c \"docker restart <container_name>\"` instantly cleans the browser state and auto-reauthenticates in ~15-20s.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Active Background Cron Task:** `task-9328` (Recurring cron: `0,30 * * * *`), fires every